Archive: util-linux-2.40.2.tar.xz
Origname: util-linux-2.40.2
Name: yolo-util-linux

    util-linux 2.40.2 for yolo (non-Fil-C) builds, containing only the
    lsfd bsearch fix.  Pristine glibc 2.44 defines a const-preserving
    bsearch macro with 5 parameters (C23), and lsfd passed a compound
    literal whose internal comma was not protected by parentheses.  The
    Fil-C glibc forks defuse __glibc_const_generic, so the Fil-C build
    does not hit this; yolo builds against pristine glibc 2.44 do.
    Same upstream fix as in util-linux.projeny:
    711bda1441561bfd2eb6d45fe0bc789535c1f1a8 (OpenEmbedded backport).
diff --git a/yolo-util-linux/misc-utils/lsfd.c b/yolo-util-linux/misc-utils/lsfd.c
--- a/yolo-util-linux/misc-utils/lsfd.c
+++ b/yolo-util-linux/misc-utils/lsfd.c
@@ -1569,7 +1569,7 @@
 		struct file *file = list_entry(f, struct file, files);
 		if (is_opened_file(file) && !file->multiplexed) {
 			int fd = file->association;
-			if (bsearch(&(struct pollfd){.fd = fd,}, local.iov_base,
+			if (bsearch((&(struct pollfd){.fd = fd,}), local.iov_base,
 				    nfds, sizeof(struct pollfd), pollfdcmp))
 				file->multiplexed = 1;
 		}
